# Codebase Memory MCP (default)

Use the `user-codebase-memory-mcp` MCP server before grep/file-by-file reads when exploring **this** codebase.

## Session start

1. If the workspace is not indexed yet, call `index_repository` with the repo root path (or rely on `auto_index`).
2. Use the indexed `project` name in every tool call that accepts `project`.

## Tool selection

| Task | Tool |
|------|------|
| Find definitions, classes, routes, symbols | `search_graph` |
| Text search enriched with graph context | `search_code` |
| Callers / callees / data flow | `trace_path` |
| Architecture, modules, hotspots, layers | `get_architecture` |
| Uncommitted change impact | `detect_changes` |
| Read a known symbol body | `get_code_snippet` (after `search_graph`) |
| Multi-hop graph patterns | `query_graph` |

## When NOT to use graph tools

- Editing a file the user already pointed to
- Config/docs-only questions with no code structure
- One-off string search in a known file path

## Fallback

If MCP is disconnected or returns empty results, fall back to `Grep` / `Read` and mention that indexing may be pending.
